        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0154" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5755: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-13T16:00:00+08:00">January 13, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 13—5:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Nanking’s January 10, 5 p.m., regarding Boxer protocol. Spanish Minister,
                    French Minister, Italian Minister, British Chargé d’Affaires and I discussed
                    this note, agreed that as Chinese asked nothing there was nothing for us to do
                    but to await instructions from our respective Governments.</p>
                <p>Other colleagues to be furnished informal suggestion contained in Peck’s last
                    paragraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
